      "claim": "Fexofenadine, the closest new zwitterionic analogue (Morgan 0.3947), has a rat Kp,uu,brain/plasma of only 0.02 after subcutaneous dosing, directly demonstrating inadequate CNS access for a piperidine-carboxylic acid zwitterion.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C21"],
      "claim": "Bepotastine, another zwitterionic piperidine-acid, had brain ISF concentrations lower than unbound plasma in mice by microdialysis, supporting poor CNS distribution for this acid/base class.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C19"],
      "claim": "Darifenacin, a large basic piperidine, showed a rat Kp,free of 0.02, indicating that lipophilic piperidine-containing molecules can still have very low unbound brain exposure.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C13"],
      "claim": "MDL 105,725, a phenolic piperidine metabolite, had a brain ECF/total plasma AUC ratio <0.25 after i.v. dosing in rats, showing restricted CNS penetration despite a piperidine scaffold.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C03"],
      "claim": "A benzimidazole-piperidine analogue without the carboxylic acid had B/Pb 2.7 in rats, but this positive CNS result does not transfer because the query's ionized acid/zwitterion adds a major permeability/efflux liability absent in this analogue.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C16"],
      "claim": "MDL 100,907, a lipophilic basic piperidine without an acid, achieved a brain ECF/total plasma AUC ratio of 1.01 in rats, but its lack of the query's zwitterionic acid makes it a poor positive model for the query.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C18"],
      "claim": "Fentanyl, a lipophilic basic piperidine, had Kp,uu,b/p 1.6 in rats, indicating net inward transport, but it lacks the carboxylic acid/zwitterionic character of the query and does not support acid-containing CNS penetration.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The query is a large zwitterionic benzimidazole-piperidine with a free carboxylic acid and basic piperidine, fully ionized at physiological pH. The most transferable new evidence is fexofenadine (Morgan 0.3947), a structurally analogous zwitterionic piperidine-acid with a rat Kp,uu,brain/plasma of only 0.02, and bepotastine, another zwitterionic piperidine-acid with brain ISF below unbound plasma. These direct CNS-exposure measurements override positive results from lipophilic basic benzimidazole/piperidine analogues lacking the acid. Passive BBB access is expected to be inadequate, and no evidence supports active uptake overcoming the charge and polarity burden.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct brain/plasma, CSF, or uptake data for the exact query or a very close zwitterionic analogue.",
    "Efflux-transporter substrate status of the query is unknown, though zwitterionic analogues are P-gp substrates.",
    "Estimated logD and pKa values may have errors, and active uptake cannot be fully excluded."
  ],
